# agent-lessons -- line-ending policy
#
# WHY THIS FILE EXISTS: the installer copies `hooks/pre-commit` into the user's
# `.git/hooks/` and it has to be executable *there*. With `core.autocrlf=true`
# (the Windows default) git rewrites text files to CRLF on checkout, and a CRLF
# shebang -- `#!/usr/bin/env sh\r` -- is the classic
# "bad interpreter: No such file or directory" on POSIX.
#
# ⚠ HONEST NOTE (guideline 08): I could NOT reproduce that failure. In Git Bash on
#   Windows both the CRLF and the LF copy exit 0, run directly as `./hook` and as
#   `sh hook`. So this file removes an ambiguity; it does not fix a measured bug.
#   It is here because it costs three lines and, if the failure ever does happen,
#   it lands on a user instead of on me.
#
# ⚠ And the reverse direction matters too: `.cmd` files are read by cmd.exe,
#   where LF-only line endings can break labels and `goto`. Do not "fix" the
#   `.cmd` rule to LF -- it is deliberate.

* text=auto

# Machine-executed scripts: force LF, everywhere, regardless of the cloner's config.
hooks/*        text eol=lf
install/*.sh   text eol=lf
*.sh           text eol=lf

# cmd.exe reads these; CRLF is the safe form there.
*.cmd          text eol=crlf
